            "result": "Found 4 email(s) matching 'study hours' in outbox (showing most relevant):\n\n\n--- Match 1 (Relevance: 0.22932903496663765) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: team@startup.com\nSubject: Weekly Standup Notes\nDate: 2025-10-06T09:00:00Z\nStatus: Sent\nBody:\nTeam,\n\nHere's a summary of this week's standup:\n\nCompleted:\n- User authentication system\n- Database optimization\n- API documentation\n\nIn Progress:\n- Frontend redesign\n- Performance testing\n\nBlockers:\n- Waiting for design assets from external team\n\nNext week's priorities will be discussed in tomorrow's planning meeting.\n\nThanks,\nYou\n\n\n--- Match 2 (Relevance: 0.21977204473383485) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: tina@enron.com\nSubject: Meeting Notes from Yesterday\nDate: 2025-10-04T15:30:00Z\nStatus: Sent\nBody:\nHi,\n\nHere are the key points from yesterday's meeting:\n\n1. Project timeline has been updated\n2. New requirements from the client\n3. Next review scheduled for Friday\n\nPlease let me know if you have any questions.\n\nBest,\nVince\n\n\n--- Match 3 (Relevance: 0.16717582081270127) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: evan@gmail.com\nSubject: Project Update - Phase 1 Complete\nDate: 2025-10-03T11:45:00Z\nStatus: Sent\nBody:\nDear Evan,\n\nI'm pleased to inform you that Phase 1 of the project has been completed successfully. The initial deliverables are ready for your review.\n\nKey achievements:\n- All requirements have been implemented\n- Testing completed with 95% pass rate\n- Documentation updated\n\nNext steps will be discussed in our scheduled call tomorrow.\n\nBest regards,\nVince\n\n\n--- Match 4 (Relevance: 0.13267774764692783) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: investor@venture.com\nSubject: Q3 Progress Report\nDate: 2025-10-01T14:20:00Z\nStatus: Sent\nBody:\nDear Investor,\n\nI'm pleased to share our Q3 progress report with you.\n\nKey Metrics:\n- User growth: +150% month-over-month\n- Revenue: $50K (target: $45K)\n- Customer satisfaction: 4.8/5.0\n\nMajor Milestones:\n- Launched mobile app\n- Secured partnership with TechCorp\n- Expanded team to 12 members\n\nWe're on track to meet our year-end goals. I'll be available for a call next week to discuss any questions you may have.\n\nBest regards,\nYou\n",
            "count": 4,
            "folder": "outbox"
          },
          "call_id": "tcall_844308f1-2f71-45cc-8f97-6106db319733"
        },
        {
          "event_id": "53b8959f-f187-4495-af0e-6d4c23ce7eeb",
          "event_type": "tool_result",
          "timestamp": "2026-02-22T03:44:52.392897+00:00",
          "session_id": "bench_527d185c",
          "tool_name": "search_emails",
          "outputs": {
            "result": "Found 4 email(s) matching 'study hours' in drafts (showing most relevant):\n\n\n--- Match 1 (Relevance: 0.18396243776674093) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: mike@enron.com\nSubject: Request for Additional Resources\nDate: 2025-10-07T10:15:00Z\nStatus: Draft\nBody:\nHi Mike,\n\nI hope this email finds you well. I'm writing to request additional resources for the current project.\n\nCurrent situation:\n- Team is working at full capacity\n- Project timeline is tight\n- Quality may be compromised without additional support\n\nRequest:\n- 2 additional developers\n- Extended deadline by 2 weeks\n- Additional budget for tools and training\n\nI'd appreciate the opportunity to discuss this further in our next meeting.\n\nBest regards,\nVince\n\n\n--- Match 2 (Relevance: 0.14392890463445668) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: hr@company.com\nSubject: Vacation Request - December\nDate: 2025-10-07T08:45:00Z\nStatus: Draft\nBody:\nHi HR Team,\n\nI would like to request vacation time for the following dates:\n\nRequested Dates: December 20-31, 2025\nTotal Days: 8 working days\n\nReason: Family holiday trip\n\nI've ensured that all my current projects will be completed before my departure, and I've arranged for coverage during my absence.\n\nPlease let me know if this request is approved or if you need any additional information.\n\nThank you,\nYou\n\n\n--- Match 3 (Relevance: 0.12749739670966148) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: vendor@supplies.com\nSubject: Contract Renewal Discussion\nDate: 2025-10-06T16:30:00Z\nStatus: Draft\nBody:\nDear Vendor Team,\n\nI hope you're doing well. I'm reaching out to discuss the renewal of our current contract which expires at the end of this month.\n\nWe've been very satisfied with your services over the past year. However, we'd like to discuss:\n\n1. Potential volume discounts for increased usage\n2. Extended support hours\n3. Additional service level agreements\n\nWould you be available for a call this week to discuss these points?\n\nLooking forward to continuing our partnership,\nVince\n\n\n--- Match 4 (Relevance: 0.11026630694491683) ---\nFrom: vince.j.kaminski@enron.com\nTo: conference@techsummit.com\nSubject: Speaker Proposal - AI Security Best Practices\nDate: 2025-10-05T13:20:00Z\nStatus: Draft\nBody:\nDear Conference Organizers,\n\nI'm writing to submit a speaker proposal for your upcoming Tech Summit 2026.\n\nProposed Topic: \"AI Security Best Practices: Protecting Your Models from Adversarial Attacks\"\n\nSession Details:\n- Duration: 45 minutes\n- Format: Presentation with Q&A\n- Target Audience: Developers and Security Professionals\n- Level: Intermediate to Advanced\n\nAbout Me:\n- 5+ years in AI security research\n- Published papers on adversarial machine learning\n- Experience with enterprise security implementations\n\nI believe this topic would be valuable for your attendees. Please let me know if you need any additional information.\n\nBest regards,\nYou\n",
